/-!
# The free resolution attached to a family of morphisms

Let `X` be an object of a category `C` and `U : ι → Over X` a family of objects over `X` (with
`ι : Type w`). For `n : ℕ` let `ℤ_𝔘[n]` be the presheaf of abelian groups on `C` freely
generated by the pairs `(y, g)` of a tuple `y : Fin (n + 1) → ι` and a morphism
`g : T ⟶ U (y 0) ×_X ⋯ ×_X U (y n)`. With the alternating sums of the face maps these form a
complex `⋯ ⟶ ℤ_𝔘[1] ⟶ ℤ_𝔘[0] ⟶ ℤ[yoneda X]` of presheaves of abelian groups in the universe
`max v w` (the presheaf of sets `yoneda X` is lifted to `Type (max v w)`), which is exact in
degrees `≥ 0`: over every object `T` it is contracted by inserting, in front of a tuple
`(y, g)`, a lift of `T ⟶ X` to one of the `U a`, chosen depending only on `T ⟶ X`.

Morphisms from `ℤ_𝔘[n]` to a presheaf `P` are the Čech cochains of degree `n` of `P`, so this
complex is used to prove that Čech complexes of injective presheaves are exact.

## Main definitions

- `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.cechFree U n`: the presheaf `ℤ_𝔘[n]`.
- `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.cechFreeD U n : ℤ_𝔘[n + 1] ⟶ ℤ_𝔘[n]`: the differential.
- `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.cechFreeAug U : ℤ_𝔘[0] ⟶ ℤ[yoneda X]`: the augmentation.

## Main statements

- `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.exact_cechFreeD`: exactness in positive degrees.
- `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.exact_cechFreeAug`: exactness in degree `0`.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe w v u

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite

namespace CategoryTheory.Presheaf

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {X : C} [HasFiniteProducts (Over X)] {ι : Type w}
  (U : ι → Over X)

variable {U}

end CategoryTheory.Presheaf
